/Title (Patient experience is only weakly linked to objective clinical quality. Readmission measures show a mild positive relationship \(r = 0.16\), mortality performance is essentially unrelated \(r = 0.01\), and safety performance is weakly negative \(r = -0.17\). Satisfaction and clinical excellence are largely independent  hospitals should be judged on both, not one as a proxy for the other.)
